2. Experimental entropy inflation =E2=80=94 AI increases the *variety* of p=
hysical
validation required =E2=80=94 *9.3/10* Thesis

A common assumption is:

better prediction -> fewer experiments

Recent evidence suggests a more interesting dynamic:

better prediction -> much larger searchable hypothesis space -> exploration
of previously ignored targets -> more heterogeneous/custom experiments

The April 2026 NBER AlphaFold study finds that experimental structure
determination did *not* collapse after AlphaFold2. Instead, research
shifted toward proteins that previously lacked structural information;
basic research on those proteins increased roughly *15=E2=80=9340%* relativ=
e to
already-characterized proteins.

That implies AI can increase *experimental entropy* even if it reduces
experiments per hypothesis.

GenScript now provides unusually direct commercial confirmation. In H1 2026
its AI-enabled drug-discovery business *doubled YoY* for a third
consecutive half-year of rapid growth. Management says AI customers
increasingly require protein engineering, biologics discovery and physical
validation; Gene-to-Protein represents ~66% of Life Science revenue.
Earlier 2026 commentary indicated roughly *70% of protein orders* were
supporting AI-driven antibody/complex-antibody discovery programs.

This is materially stronger evidence than the earlier generic =E2=80=9CDNA
synthesis is the compiler=E2=80=9D thesis. The scarce layer is becoming *ra=
pid
custom design-build-test throughput for off-distribution biological objects=
*
.
Candidate exposure

*GenScript Biotech (1548.HK <http://1548.HK>)* is the obvious direct
exposure, but no longer uncrowded. The stock=E2=80=99s market cap is around
HK$70=E2=80=9375B and has nearly doubled over the last year; current screen=
s imply
~115x forward earnings. The business signal is excellent; the entry price
is not.

Better alpha may sit beneath GenScript in suppliers of high-throughput
purification, custom reagents, assay development, specialty resins and
low-volume/high-mix automation.
Kernel primitive

Define:

ExperimentalEntropy =3D diversity of distinct physical protocols / validate=
d
hypothesis

and

PhysicalizationTax =3D cost + latency of turning a computational candidate
into a verified physical object

The best businesses may have increasing revenue when *candidate diversity*,
not candidate count, rises.
Falsifiers

   - AI converges biological programs onto fewer standardized modalities
   rather than widening target diversity.
   - In-silico validation improves enough that physical candidate counts
   fall faster than search-space expansion.
   - GenScript=E2=80=99s AI growth proves to be biotech-cycle recovery rath=
er than
   a persistent AI-specific mix shift.

Sources:

   - NBER AlphaFold paper: https://www.nber.org/papers/w35143
   - GenScript H1 2026:
   https://www.biopharmaapac.com/company-results/120/8336/genscript-ceo-she=
rry-shao-sees-ai-enabled-drug-discovery-as-key-growth-engine-after-strong-h=
1-2026.html

3. Rare-failure telemetry becomes a negative-data asset class =E2=80=94 *8.=
9/10*
Thesis

As autonomous systems get better, ordinary-success data gets cheaper
while *real
failures become rarer and more valuable*. The training objective shifts
from =E2=80=9Clearn normal operation=E2=80=9D to =E2=80=9Cfind the 1-in-100=
k event that still kills
the system.=E2=80=9D

2026 autonomous-vehicle research shows adaptive stress testing and
diffusion-based failure sampling can discover collision modes that ordinary
Monte Carlo simulation misses. Manufacturing research reaches the same
structural problem: mature systems generate extremely imbalanced failure
datasets.

This creates a new data-moat hierarchy:

success telemetry < synthetic failures < expert-labelled real failures <
longitudinal failure + remediation histories

The most valuable industrial datasets may therefore belong to businesses
that have spent decades inspecting things that break.
Obscure public exposure: MISTRAS Group (NYSE: MG)

MISTRAS is a ~$0.6B market-cap asset-integrity/NDT company spanning
aerospace, power, infrastructure, industrial facilities and pipelines. Its
proprietary software centralizes inspection and integrity data for
predictive analytics and benchmarking.

The current business is also showing the exact physical bottlenecks the
thesis predicts: in Q2 management said *Aerospace & Defense demand was
temporarily outpacing testing capacity*, and data-center/power investment
was increasing demand for QA, inspection, commissioning and asset-integrity
work. Q2 revenue grew 4.2%, operating income 53.6%, and adjusted EBITDA 7%.

At roughly *16=E2=80=9318x forward earnings*, MG is much cheaper than most =
explicit
AI-data companies, although the stock has already roughly doubled over the
last year and remains labor-intensive with debt.

The optionality is not that MISTRAS suddenly becomes an AI software
company. It is that decades of failure/inspection histories gain value as
industrial models need rare, labelled, physical-ground-truth events.
Kernel primitive

NegativeDataDensity =3D economically meaningful labelled failures / unit of
normal telemetry

FailureHistoryUniqueness =3D difficulty of recreating dataset without waiti=
ng
for real-world failures

High FailureHistoryUniqueness should be treated as a moat even when the
current company monetizes it poorly.
Falsifiers

   - Synthetic stress testing reproduces real rare-event distributions
   sufficiently well.
   - Customers own all inspection data and prevent cross-customer model
   learning.
   - MISTRAS cannot productize or monetize its historical data beyond
   labor-heavy services.

Sources:

   - Commercial AV rare-event research:
   https://www.max-robotics.com/en/research/publications/cmrvvwfnn0045qz1m3=
dyvaxz7
   - MISTRAS Q2 2026:
   https://mistrasgroup.gcs-web.com/news-releases/news-release-details/mist=
ras-announces-second-quarter-and-first-half-2026-results
   - MISTRAS 2025 10-K summary:
   https://www.publicnow.com/view/232B577199304589270E6ABCB6FD96153404F906

4. O-ring automation formally validates scarcity migration =E2=80=94 *8.7/1=
0,
kernel-level rather than stock-specific*

The January 2026 NBER paper *O-Ring Automation* is unusually important for
our framework. It models production where task qualities multiply rather
than add. In these systems, smoothly improving automation can trigger
discrete bundled adoption =E2=80=94 and automating some tasks can *increase=
 the
value of the remaining human or physical bottleneck tasks*.

This is essentially a formal economic foundation for scarcity migration.

If output is approximately:

Q =3D q1 =C3=97 q2 =C3=97 ... =C3=97 qn

then raising nine factors toward infinity does not make the tenth
irrelevant; it increases the shadow value of improving the tenth.

This gives a general screen:

   1. Identify workflows with multiplicative quality/completion constraints=
.
   2. Estimate which stages AI collapses first.
   3. Recalculate the marginal economic value of the untouched stage.
   4. Buy the provider of that stage *before revenue growth becomes obvious=
*
   .

This is more useful than =E2=80=9CAI exposure=E2=80=9D screens because it p=
redicts winners
that have almost no AI narrative at all.
New kernel primitive

O_Ring_Gating_Leverage_i =3D downstream value unlocked by marginal
improvement in task i / cost of task i

Then model its derivative after upstream automation:

d(O_Ring_Gating_Leverage_i) / d(AI capability)

The largest positive derivatives are the hidden beneficiaries.

Source:

   - NBER O-Ring Automation: https://www.nber.org/papers/w34639

Ranking

   1. *Mandatory physical identity / DPP infrastructure =E2=80=94 9.5*
   2. *Experimental entropy / custom biological physicalization =E2=80=94 9=
.3*
   3. *Rare-failure telemetry / negative-data asset class =E2=80=94 8.9*
   4. *O-ring gating leverage as a general alpha screen =E2=80=94 8.7*

Best current tradable setup

*AVY* looks strongest on combined thesis quality, current evidence and
valuation. The DPP layer is newly operational rather than hypothetical, the
first mandatory deadline is only ~5 months away, Avery already owns both
the physical-ID layer and associated software, and ~16=E2=80=9317x forward =
earnings
leaves much less narrative premium than PI.
Best asymmetric research target

*MG* is stranger and less consensus. The key question is whether its
proprietary integrity/failure histories can become reusable
machine-learning assets rather than remaining trapped inside inspection
services. If yes, the market is valuing a potentially scarce negative-data
corpus as a conventional industrial-services business.
Most important kernel update

Add a distinction between *state data* and *state identity*. Autonomous
agents need both:

WorldStateReliability =3D identity certainty =C3=97 state freshness =C3=97 =
provenance =C3=97
permission

If identity certainty is zero, arbitrarily intelligent agents still cannot
safely map a digital decision onto the correct physical object.

