2. Experimental entropy inflation =E2=80=94 AI increases the <em>variety</e=
m> of physical validation required =E2=80=94 <strong>9.3/10</strong>

Thesis
<p>A common assumption is:</p>
<p><code>better prediction -&gt; fewer experiments</code></p>
<p>Recent evidence suggests a more interesting dynamic:</p>
<p><code>better prediction -&gt; much larger searchable hypothesis space -&=
gt; exploration of previously ignored targets -&gt; more heterogeneous/cust=
om experiments</code></p>
<p>The April 2026 NBER AlphaFold study finds that experimental structure de=
termination did <strong>not</strong> collapse after AlphaFold2. Instead, re=
search shifted toward proteins that previously lacked structural informatio=
n; basic research on those proteins increased roughly <strong>15=E2=80=9340=
%</strong> relative to already-characterized proteins.</p>
<p>That implies AI can increase <strong>experimental entropy</strong> even =
if it reduces experiments per hypothesis.</p>
<p>GenScript now provides unusually direct commercial confirmation. In H1 2=
026 its AI-enabled drug-discovery business <strong>doubled YoY</strong> for=
 a third consecutive half-year of rapid growth. Management says AI customer=
s increasingly require protein engineering, biologics discovery and physica=
l validation; Gene-to-Protein represents ~66% of Life Science revenue. Earl=
ier 2026 commentary indicated roughly <strong>70% of protein orders</strong=
> were supporting AI-driven antibody/complex-antibody discovery programs.</=
p>
<p>This is materially stronger evidence than the earlier generic =E2=80=9CD=
NA synthesis is the compiler=E2=80=9D thesis. The scarce layer is becoming =
<strong>rapid custom design-build-test throughput for off-distribution biol=
ogical objects</strong>.</p>

